# OpenRouter

The one door to a language model: an OpenAI-shaped chat-completions request
through OpenRouter, paid for from the contributor's own key and budget.

Everything here is pure — building the request, reading the reply, reading the
price list, and the money arithmetic. The call itself is made by `host.lg`, which
is also the only place the API key is read; the key goes into one request header
and nowhere else (never a trail entry, never a log line, never the coordinator).

The money rule is RESERVE, THEN RECONCILE. Before a call, the worst case it can
cost is reserved against the budget, and a call whose worst case does not fit is
not made — the worker stops honestly instead of overspending. After the call,
the reservation is replaced by what the call actually cost: the cost OpenRouter
reports when it reports one, else the tokens it reports at the listed price.

Import Wire.
Import Shared.
Import Submission.

## Note
One message of a conversation: `system`, `user` or `assistant`, and its text.

## A ChatMessage has:
    a role, which is Text.
    a content, which is Text.

## Note
What is asked of a model. `temperatureBp` is the sampling temperature in basis
points (2,000 is 0.2), so a strategy stores it as an integer like every other
score.

## A ChatRequest has:
    a model, which is Text.
    a messages, which is Seq of ChatMessage.
    a maxTokens, which is Int.
    a temperatureBp, which is Int.

## Note
What a model answered, read. `costMicros` is OpenRouter's own reported cost,
rounded up to a micro-dollar, when the reply carries one; `usageKnown` says
whether the reply reported its token counts at all.

## A ChatReply has:
    an id, which is Text.
    a model, which is Text.
    a content, which is Text.
    a finishReason, which is Text.
    a usageKnown, which is Bool.
    a promptTokens, which is Int.
    a completionTokens, which is Int.
    a costMicros, which is Option of Int.

## Note
A model's price, as the factory computes with it: micro-dollars per million
tokens (OpenRouter's `"0.0000025"` dollars a token is 2,500,000), plus a flat
price per request. Where OpenRouter lists a higher tier for long prompts
(`overrides`), the HIGHEST price is kept, because a reservation is a worst case.
`maxCompletionTokens` is `0` when OpenRouter does not say.

## A ModelPrice has:
    an id, which is Text.
    a promptPerMTok, which is Int.
    a completionPerMTok, which is Int.
    a requestMicros, which is Int.
    a contextLength, which is Int.
    a maxCompletionTokens, which is Int.

## Note
A contributor's budget: the limit they set, what calls have cost, and what is held
for calls in flight.

## A Budget has:
    a limitMicros, which is Int.
    a spentMicros, which is Int.
    a reservedMicros, which is Int.

## Note
Where requests go.

## To chatCompletionsUrl () -> Text:
    Return "https://openrouter.ai/api/v1/chat/completions".

## Note
Where the price list is. It needs no key.

## To modelsUrl () -> Text:
    Return "https://openrouter.ai/api/v1/models".

## Note
The headers of a request: the contributor's key as a bearer token, and the two
attribution headers OpenRouter asks applications to send.

## To openRouterHeaders (apiKey: Text) -> Map of Text to Text:
    Let mutable h be a new Map of Text to Text.
    Set h at "Authorization" to "Bearer " + apiKey.
    Set h at "Content-Type" to "application/json".
    Set h at "HTTP-Referer" to "https://macsad.com".
    Set h at "X-Title" to "MaCSad factory".
    Return h.

## Note
JSON building blocks, so a request is written as the structure it is.

## To jstr (s: Text) -> Json:
    Return a new JStr with s s.

## Note
A JSON integer.

## To jint (n: Int) -> Json:
    Return a new JNum with n n.

## Note
A JSON object member.

## To jfield (key: Text, v: Json) -> JEntry:
    Return a new JEntry with key key and val v.

## Note
Basis points as the exact JSON decimal they stand for: `2000` is `0.2`, `10000` is
`1`, `15` is `0.0015`.

## To bpDecimal (bp: Int) -> Json:
    If bp % 10000 is equal to 0:
        Return a new JNum with n (bp / 10000).
    Let mutable m be bp.
    Let mutable sc be 0 - 4.
    While m % 10 is equal to 0:
        Set m to m / 10.
        Set sc to sc + 1.
    Return a new JDec with mant m and scale sc.

## Note
The request body. `usage.include` asks OpenRouter to report the call's cost in the
reply, which is what reconciliation reads. The members are in a fixed order and
the serialization is canonical, so the body — and the prompt hash taken over it —
is the same on every machine.

## To chatRequestJson (r: ChatRequest) -> Text:
    Let mutable msgs be a new Seq of Json.
    Repeat for m in r's messages:
        Push (a new JObj with entries [jfield("role", jstr(m's role)), jfield("content", jstr(m's content))]) to msgs.
    Let usage be a new JObj with entries [jfield("include", a new JBool with b true)].
    Let body be a new JObj with entries [jfield("model", jstr(r's model)), jfield("messages", a new JArr with elems msgs), jfield("max_tokens", jint(r's maxTokens)), jfield("temperature", bpDecimal(r's temperatureBp)), jfield("usage", usage)].
    Return jsonSerialize(body).

## Note
The prompt hash: the SHA-256 of the exact request body. Two calls with the same
hash asked the same model the same thing with the same budget of tokens, which is
what the replay provider keys its recordings by.

## To promptSha (r: ChatRequest) -> Text:
    Return sha256Hex(chatRequestJson(r)).

## Note
The shape of a successful reply that the factory reads; the rest is ignored.

## To chatReplyShape () -> Seq of Text:
    Return ["id:text", "model:text", "choices:array"].

## Note
The message of an error reply (`{"error": {"code": 402, "message": "…"}}`), or `""`.

## To errorOfReply (v: Json) -> Text:
    If jsonHas(v, "error") is equal to false:
        Return "".
    Let e be jsonGet(v, "error").
    Let message be textAt(e, "message").
    Inspect jsonGet(e, "code"):
        When JNum (code):
            Return "OpenRouter error {code}: {message}".
        Otherwise:
            Return "OpenRouter error: {message}".
    Return "OpenRouter error: {message}".

## Note
A chat-completions reply read: the first choice's message content and finish
reason, and the usage — token counts and, when present, the reported cost in
dollars, rounded up to a micro-dollar.

## To parseChatReply (text: Text) -> Result of ChatReply and Text:
    Inspect parseStrict(text):
        When Err (e):
            Return a new Err with error "the reply is not JSON: " + e.
        When Ok (v):
            Let failure be errorOfReply(v).
            If failure is not equal to "":
                Return a new Err with error failure.
            Let problem be openShapeProblem(v, chatReplyShape()).
            If problem is not equal to "":
                Return a new Err with error "the reply is not a chat completion: " + problem.
            Let mutable content be "".
            Let mutable finish be "".
            Inspect jsonGet(v, "choices"):
                When JArr (choices):
                    If length of choices is equal to 0:
                        Return a new Err with error "the reply has no choices".
                    Let first be item 1 of choices.
                    Let message be jsonGet(first, "message").
                    Inspect jsonGet(message, "content"):
                        When JStr (s):
                            Set content to s.
                        Otherwise:
                            Return a new Err with error "the first choice has no text content".
                    Set finish to textAt(first, "finish_reason").
                Otherwise:
                    Return a new Err with error "the reply has no choices".
            Let usage be jsonGet(v, "usage").
            Let known be openShapeProblem(usage, ["prompt_tokens:int", "completion_tokens:int"]) is equal to "".
            Let mutable cost: Option of Int be none.
            If jsonHas(usage, "cost"):
                Inspect jsonScaledCeil(jsonGet(usage, "cost"), 6):
                    When Ok (micros):
                        Set cost to some micros.
                    When Err (e):
                        Return a new Err with error "the reply's cost is unreadable: " + e.
            Return a new Ok with value (a new ChatReply with id textAt(v, "id") and model textAt(v, "model") and content content and finishReason finish and usageKnown known and promptTokens intAt(usage, "prompt_tokens") and completionTokens intAt(usage, "completion_tokens") and costMicros cost).
    Return a new Err with error "unreadable reply".

## Note
One listed price, per million tokens, rounded up; a negative listing (OpenRouter
writes `"-1"` for a router whose price depends on where it routes) is refused,
because such a model has no worst case to reserve.

## To pricePerMTok (v: Json, what: Text) -> Result of Int and Text:
    Inspect v:
        When JStr (s):
            If startsWith(trim(s), "-"):
                Return a new Err with error "the {what} price is not fixed ({s})".
            Return decimalTextScaledCeil(s, 12).
        When JNull:
            Return a new Ok with value 0.
        Otherwise:
            Return a new Err with error "the {what} price is not a decimal string".
    Return a new Err with error "unreadable price".

## Note
The larger of two integers.

## To maxInt (a: Int, b: Int) -> Int:
    If a is greater than b:
        Return a.
    Return b.

## Note
A model's price from its entry in OpenRouter's model list: base prompt and
completion prices, raised to the highest `overrides` tier, the per-request
price rounded up to a micro-dollar, and the context limits.

## To modelPriceOf (m: Json) -> Result of ModelPrice and Text:
    Let id be textAt(m, "id").
    Let pricing be jsonGet(m, "pricing").
    Inspect pricePerMTok(jsonGet(pricing, "prompt"), "prompt"):
        When Err (e):
            Return a new Err with error id + ": " + e.
        When Ok (prompt):
            Inspect pricePerMTok(jsonGet(pricing, "completion"), "completion"):
                When Err (e):
                    Return a new Err with error id + ": " + e.
                When Ok (completion):
                    Let mutable p be prompt.
                    Let mutable c be completion.
                    Inspect jsonGet(pricing, "overrides"):
                        When JArr (tiers):
                            Repeat for tier in tiers:
                                Inspect pricePerMTok(jsonGet(tier, "prompt"), "prompt"):
                                    When Ok (tp):
                                        Set p to maxInt(p, tp).
                                    When Err (e):
                                        Return a new Err with error id + ": " + e.
                                Inspect pricePerMTok(jsonGet(tier, "completion"), "completion"):
                                    When Ok (tc):
                                        Set c to maxInt(c, tc).
                                    When Err (e):
                                        Return a new Err with error id + ": " + e.
                        Otherwise:
                            Let ignored be p.
                    Let mutable request be 0.
                    If jsonHas(pricing, "request"):
                        Inspect pricePerMTok(jsonGet(pricing, "request"), "request"):
                            When Ok (perMillion):
                                Set request to ceilDiv(perMillion, 1000000).
                            When Err (e):
                                Return a new Err with error id + ": " + e.
                    Let top be jsonGet(m, "top_provider").
                    Return a new Ok with value (a new ModelPrice with id id and promptPerMTok p and completionPerMTok c and requestMicros request and contextLength intAt(m, "context_length") and maxCompletionTokens intAt(top, "max_completion_tokens")).
    Return a new Err with error id + ": unreadable price".

## Note
The price of `modelId` in an OpenRouter model list document, or why there is none.

## To priceOf (modelsJson: Text, modelId: Text) -> Result of ModelPrice and Text:
    Inspect parseStrict(modelsJson):
        When Err (e):
            Return a new Err with error "the model list is not JSON: " + e.
        When Ok (v):
            Inspect jsonGet(v, "data"):
                When JArr (models):
                    Repeat for m in models:
                        If textAt(m, "id") is equal to modelId:
                            Return modelPriceOf(m).
                    Return a new Err with error "OpenRouter lists no model {modelId}".
                Otherwise:
                    Return a new Err with error "the model list has no data array".
    Return a new Err with error "unreadable model list".

## Note
`a / b` rounded up, for positive `b`.

## To ceilDiv (a: Int, b: Int) -> Int:
    Let q be a / b.
    If a % b is greater than 0:
        Return q + 1.
    Return q.

## Note
An upper bound on the prompt tokens of a request, without a tokenizer: every token
is at least one byte, so a message cannot be more tokens than it has bytes. Each
message is also charged 16 tokens for the role and the framing around it. The
bound is loose — prose is about four bytes a token — and that is the point: a
reservation is a worst case, and reconciliation returns the difference.

## To promptTokenBound (r: ChatRequest) -> Int:
    Let mutable total be 0.
    Repeat for m in r's messages:
        Set total to total + length of text_bytes(m's content) + length of text_bytes(m's role) + 16.
    Return total.

## Note
The most a request can cost: every prompt token at the highest prompt price, the
whole `maxTokens` allowance at the highest completion price, and the per-request
price, rounded up to a micro-dollar.

## To reservationMicros (p: ModelPrice, r: ChatRequest) -> Int:
    Let tokens be promptTokenBound(r) * p's promptPerMTok + r's maxTokens * p's completionPerMTok.
    Return ceilDiv(tokens, 1000000) + p's requestMicros.

## Note
What a finished call cost: OpenRouter's reported cost when there is one; else the
reported tokens at the listed price; else — a reply that reports nothing — the
whole reservation, since nothing smaller can be shown to be enough.

## To actualCostMicros (p: ModelPrice, reply: ChatReply, reserved: Int) -> Int:
    Inspect reply's costMicros:
        When Some (c):
            Return c.
        When None:
            If reply's usageKnown:
                Return ceilDiv(reply's promptTokens * p's promptPerMTok + reply's completionTokens * p's completionPerMTok, 1000000) + p's requestMicros.
            Return reserved.
    Return reserved.

## Note
A fresh budget of `limitMicros`.

## To newBudget (limitMicros: Int) -> Budget:
    Return a new Budget with limitMicros limitMicros and spentMicros 0 and reservedMicros 0.

## Note
What is left to reserve.

## To budgetLeft (b: Budget) -> Int:
    Return b's limitMicros - b's spentMicros - b's reservedMicros.

## Note
The budget with `amount` held for a call, or the honest stop: the reason the call
must not be made. The stop is a normal outcome, written to the trail; the worker
reports what it spent and ends.

## To reserve (b: Budget, amount: Int) -> Result of Budget and Text:
    If amount is greater than budgetLeft(b):
        Return a new Err with error "budget stop: the call may cost up to " + formatMicros(amount) + ", and " + formatMicros(budgetLeft(b)) + " of " + formatMicros(b's limitMicros) + " is left".
    Let mutable out be b.
    Set out's reservedMicros to b's reservedMicros + amount.
    Return a new Ok with value out.

## Note
The budget after a call that held `reserved` and cost `actual`: the hold is
released and the actual cost is spent.

## To settle (b: Budget, reserved: Int, actual: Int) -> Budget:
    Let mutable out be b.
    Set out's reservedMicros to b's reservedMicros - reserved.
    Set out's spentMicros to b's spentMicros + actual.
    Return out.

## Note
A request for the tests below.

## To sampleRequest () -> ChatRequest:
    Return a new ChatRequest with model "openai/gpt-4o-mini" and messages [a new ChatMessage with role "system" and content "You write LOGOS kernel proofs.", a new ChatMessage with role "user" and content "Prove goal."] and maxTokens 1000 and temperatureBp 2000.

## Note
A chat-completions reply in the shape OpenRouter documents, with its usage and
its reported cost.

## To sampleReply () -> Text:
    Return "{{\"id\":\"gen-1732300000-abc\",\"provider\":\"OpenAI\",\"model\":\"openai/gpt-4o-mini\",\"object\":\"chat.completion\",\"created\":1732300000,\"choices\":[{{\"logprobs\":null,\"finish_reason\":\"stop\",\"native_finish_reason\":\"stop\",\"index\":0,\"message\":{{\"role\":\"assistant\",\"content\":\"```logos-kernel\\nTheorem proof_of_goal : goal := by intro n; rfl.\\n```\\nSummary: tried rfl.\",\"refusal\":null,\"reasoning\":null}}}}],\"usage\":{{\"prompt_tokens\":1200,\"completion_tokens\":85,\"total_tokens\":1285,\"cost\":0.0002310,\"is_byok\":false,\"prompt_tokens_details\":{{\"cached_tokens\":0}},\"completion_tokens_details\":{{\"reasoning_tokens\":0}}}}}}".

## Note
Three entries of OpenRouter's public model list, as `GET /api/v1/models` returned
them on 2026-11-22 (only the fields the factory reads kept): a model with a
long-prompt tier, a plain one, and a router whose price is not fixed. The same
bytes are in `tests/fixtures/openrouter/models.sample.json`.

## To sampleModels () -> Text:
    Return "{{\"data\":[{{\"id\":\"google/gemini-2.5-pro\",\"name\":\"Google: Gemini 2.5 Pro\",\"context_length\":1048576,\"pricing\":{{\"prompt\":\"0.00000125\",\"completion\":\"0.00001\",\"image\":\"0.00000125\",\"audio\":\"0.00000125\",\"input_audio_cache\":\"0.000000125\",\"web_search\":\"0.014\",\"internal_reasoning\":\"0.00001\",\"input_cache_read\":\"0.000000125\",\"input_cache_write\":\"0.000000375\",\"overrides\":[{{\"min_prompt_tokens\":200000,\"prompt\":\"0.0000025\",\"completion\":\"0.000015\",\"audio\":\"0.0000025\",\"input_audio_cache\":\"0.00000025\",\"input_cache_read\":\"0.00000025\"}}]}},\"top_provider\":{{\"context_length\":1048576,\"max_completion_tokens\":65536,\"is_moderated\":false}}}},{{\"id\":\"openai/gpt-4o-mini\",\"name\":\"OpenAI: GPT-4o-mini\",\"context_length\":128000,\"pricing\":{{\"prompt\":\"0.00000015\",\"completion\":\"0.0000006\",\"input_cache_read\":\"0.000000075\"}},\"top_provider\":{{\"context_length\":128000,\"max_completion_tokens\":16384,\"is_moderated\":true}}}},{{\"id\":\"openrouter/auto\",\"name\":\"Auto Router\",\"context_length\":2000000,\"pricing\":{{\"prompt\":\"-1\",\"completion\":\"-1\"}},\"top_provider\":{{\"context_length\":null,\"max_completion_tokens\":null,\"is_moderated\":false}}}}]}}".

## Test: a request body is canonical JSON in a fixed order

Expect that chatRequestJson(sampleRequest()) is equal to "{{\"model\":\"openai/gpt-4o-mini\",\"messages\":[{{\"role\":\"system\",\"content\":\"You write LOGOS kernel proofs.\"}},{{\"role\":\"user\",\"content\":\"Prove goal.\"}}],\"max_tokens\":1000,\"temperature\":0.2,\"usage\":{{\"include\":true}}}}".
Expect that jsonValid(chatRequestJson(sampleRequest())) is equal to true.

## Test: a message with quotes and newlines is escaped, not broken

Let r be a new ChatRequest with model "m" and messages [a new ChatMessage with role "user" and content "line \"one\"\nline two"] and maxTokens 5 and temperatureBp 0.
Let body be jsonParse(chatRequestJson(r)).
Expect that jsonSerialize(jsonGet(body, "temperature")) is equal to "0".
Inspect jsonGet(body, "messages"):
    When JArr (ms):
        Expect that textAt(item 1 of ms, "content") is equal to "line \"one\"\nline two".
    Otherwise:
        Expect that "an array" is equal to "something else".

## Test: temperatures are exact decimals

For each of these cases:

| bp    | shown    |
|-------|----------|
| 0     | "0"      |
| 2000  | "0.2"    |
| 10000 | "1"      |
| 15    | "0.0015" |
| 12500 | "1.25"   |

Expect that jsonSerialize(bpDecimal(bp)) is equal to shown.

## Test: the prompt hash is the hash of the exact body

Expect that promptSha(sampleRequest()) is equal to sha256Hex(chatRequestJson(sampleRequest())).
Let mutable other be sampleRequest().
Set other's temperatureBp to 2001.
Expect that promptSha(other) is not equal to promptSha(sampleRequest()).

## Test: the key goes into the Authorization header and nowhere else

Let h be openRouterHeaders("sk-or-test").
Expect that item "Authorization" of h is equal to "Bearer sk-or-test".
Expect that item "Content-Type" of h is equal to "application/json".
Expect that chatRequestJson(sampleRequest()) contains "sk-or-test" is equal to false.

## Test: a reply yields its content, finish reason, tokens and cost

Inspect parseChatReply(sampleReply()):
    When Ok (r):
        Expect that r's content is equal to "```logos-kernel\nTheorem proof_of_goal : goal := by intro n; rfl.\n```\nSummary: tried rfl.".
        Expect that r's finishReason is equal to "stop".
        Expect that r's promptTokens is equal to 1200.
        Expect that r's completionTokens is equal to 85.
        Expect that r's costMicros is equal to some 231.
        Expect that r's usageKnown is equal to true.
        Expect that (extractSubmission(r's content))'s block is equal to "Theorem proof_of_goal : goal := by intro n; rfl.".
    When Err (e):
        Expect that e is equal to "no error".

## Test: an error reply is an error, with its code

Inspect parseChatReply("{{\"error\":{{\"code\":402,\"message\":\"Insufficient credits\"}}}}"):
    When Ok (r):
        Expect that r's content is equal to "refused".
    When Err (e):
        Expect that e is equal to "OpenRouter error 402: Insufficient credits".

## Test: a reply without choices or text is refused

Inspect parseChatReply("{{\"id\":\"g\",\"model\":\"m\",\"choices\":[]}}"):
    When Ok (r):
        Expect that r's content is equal to "refused".
    When Err (e):
        Expect that e is equal to "the reply has no choices".
Inspect parseChatReply("{{\"id\":\"g\",\"model\":\"m\",\"choices\":[{{\"message\":{{\"content\":null}}}}]}}"):
    When Ok (r):
        Expect that r's content is equal to "refused".
    When Err (e):
        Expect that e is equal to "the first choice has no text content".

## Test: a reply that reports no usage is still read

Inspect parseChatReply("{{\"id\":\"g\",\"model\":\"m\",\"choices\":[{{\"finish_reason\":\"length\",\"message\":{{\"content\":\"partial\"}}}}]}}"):
    When Ok (r):
        Expect that r's usageKnown is equal to false.
        Expect that r's costMicros is none.
        Expect that r's finishReason is equal to "length".
    When Err (e):
        Expect that e is equal to "no error".

## Test: prices are read per million tokens, at the highest tier

Inspect priceOf(sampleModels(), "google/gemini-2.5-pro"):
    When Ok (p):
        Expect that p's promptPerMTok is equal to 2500000.
        Expect that p's completionPerMTok is equal to 15000000.
        Expect that p's requestMicros is equal to 0.
        Expect that p's maxCompletionTokens is equal to 65536.
        Expect that p's contextLength is equal to 1048576.
    When Err (e):
        Expect that e is equal to "no error".
Inspect priceOf(sampleModels(), "openai/gpt-4o-mini"):
    When Ok (p):
        Expect that p's promptPerMTok is equal to 150000.
        Expect that p's completionPerMTok is equal to 600000.
    When Err (e):
        Expect that e is equal to "no error".

## Test: a model without a fixed price cannot be reserved for

Inspect priceOf(sampleModels(), "openrouter/auto"):
    When Ok (p):
        Expect that p's id is equal to "refused".
    When Err (e):
        Expect that e is equal to "openrouter/auto: the prompt price is not fixed (-1)".
Inspect priceOf(sampleModels(), "nobody/nothing"):
    When Ok (p):
        Expect that p's id is equal to "refused".
    When Err (e):
        Expect that e is equal to "OpenRouter lists no model nobody/nothing".

## Test: the prompt bound charges every byte as a token

Expect that promptTokenBound(sampleRequest()) is equal to 83.

## Test: a reservation is the worst case, and reconciliation the actual cost

Inspect priceOf(sampleModels(), "openai/gpt-4o-mini"):
    When Ok (p):
        Let held be reservationMicros(p, sampleRequest()).
        Expect that held is equal to 613.
        Inspect parseChatReply(sampleReply()):
            When Ok (reply):
                Expect that actualCostMicros(p, reply, held) is equal to 231.
                Let mutable unreported be reply.
                Set unreported's costMicros to none.
                Expect that actualCostMicros(p, unreported, held) is equal to 231.
                Set unreported's usageKnown to false.
                Expect that actualCostMicros(p, unreported, held) is equal to 613.
            When Err (e):
                Expect that e is equal to "no error".
    When Err (e):
        Expect that e is equal to "no error".

## Test: a budget holds, settles and stops honestly

Let b be newBudget(5000000).
Inspect reserve(b, 613):
    When Ok (held):
        Expect that held's reservedMicros is equal to 613.
        Let done be settle(held, 613, 231).
        Expect that done's reservedMicros is equal to 0.
        Expect that done's spentMicros is equal to 231.
        Expect that budgetLeft(done) is equal to 4999769.
    When Err (e):
        Expect that e is equal to "no error".
Inspect reserve(newBudget(500), 613):
    When Ok (held):
        Expect that held's reservedMicros is equal to -1.
    When Err (e):
        Expect that e is equal to "budget stop: the call may cost up to $0.000613, and $0.000500 of $0.000500 is left".

## Test: a budget never goes negative through reservations

For all integers limit and a and b:
    Let mutable budget be newBudget(foldTo(limit, 1000000)).
    Inspect reserve(budget, foldTo(a, 1000000)):
        When Ok (h1):
            Set budget to h1.
        When Err (e):
            Let ignored be e.
    Inspect reserve(budget, foldTo(b, 1000000)):
        When Ok (h2):
            Set budget to h2.
        When Err (e):
            Let ignored be e.
    Expect that budgetLeft(budget) is at least 0.

## Test: the embedded model list is the recorded fixture

This test may use the real filesystem.
Inspect read("tests/fixtures/openrouter/models.sample.json"):
    When Ok (text):
        Expect that trimEnd(text) is equal to sampleModels().
    When Err (e):
        Expect that e is equal to "readable".
